('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000339', 'reading', 11, '{"passage": "A professional email needs a consistent formal tone from start to finish. Before sending, always proofread the message for errors. When you know the reader''s name, closings like \"sincerely\" or \"best regards\" work well; if you do not, \"to whom it may concern\" is the standard opening. Above all, the tone should stay cordial.", "translation": "Um e-mail profissional precisa de um tom formal consistente do início ao fim. Antes de enviar, sempre revise a mensagem em busca de erros. Quando você sabe o nome do leitor, fechamentos como \"sincerely\" ou \"best regards\" funcionam bem; se não sabe, \"to whom it may concern\" é a abertura padrão. Acima de tudo, o tom deve permanecer cordial.", "question": "What should you always do before sending a professional email, according to the text?", "options": ["Add cc", "Proofread it", "Reschedule it"], "correct_index": 1}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000339', 'listening', 12, '{"audio_text": "Business emails usually require a formal tone. Always proofread your email before sending it. She closed the message with Best regards.", "question": "What should you always do before sending, according to the audio?", "options": ["Add a subject line", "Proofread the email", "Attach a document"], "correct_index": 1}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000339', 'dictation', 13, '{"audio_text": "Always proofread your email before sending it.", "expected": "Always proofread your email before sending it."}'),
